{
  "run_id": "PMC13114876__expert_context__oracle_targetpack_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The coupled tribo-corrosion response of high-entropy alloys is governed primarily by the integrity of a dynamic passive oxide film.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann",
        "PMC9960858::web::019::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical sliding periodically ruptures the passive film, after which chemical re-passivation reforms it.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann",
        "PMC9960858::web::019::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing-induced increases in hardness and microstructural density can improve resistance to passive-film destruction and tribo-corrosion damage.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron microalloying can generate in situ TiB2 particles and increase alloy hardness and wear resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A baseline HEA in 3.5 wt.% NaCl has a passive oxide film that provides partial corrosion protection.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing at approximately 800 °C is a suitable intervention for producing the proposed enhanced microstructure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The balance between film destruction and re-passivation determines the overall tribo-corrosion degradation rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann",
        "PMC9960858::web::019::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adhesion, plastic deformation, and frictional thermal effects contribute to passive-film destruction during sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::019::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased hardness and fine secondary phases such as TiB2 reduce passive-film rupture.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased hardness and TiB2 particles promote faster re-passivation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will show smaller open-circuit-potential fluctuations than the baseline alloy during sliding.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have a lower coefficient of friction than the baseline alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have lower total degradation, with both wear and corrosion components suppressed.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::013::3_4_tribocorrosion_performance_after_ann",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted benefit should hold at moderate loads and sliding speeds but may fail under sufficiently severe mechanical conditions because film reformation cannot compensate for destruction.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::019::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted benefit may fail in media too aggressive to permit effective re-passivation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled comparison should test baseline and modified samples under identical reciprocating-sliding conditions in 3.5 wt.% NaCl while monitoring OCP, friction, and wear volume.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain statistically significant reductions in OCP fluctuations, friction coefficient, and wear volume would falsify the proposed oxide-film-stability hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
